What are Coal Pulverizers for Boilers?
Coal pulverizers are mechanical devices engineered to grind raw coal into fine powder, which is subsequently injected into boiler furnaces as pulverized fuel for power generation and industrial heating applications. These systems are indispensable components in coal-fired power plants and heavy industries, as they dramatically increase the surface area of coal particles, enabling more complete and efficient combustion with improved heat release and reduced particulate emissions. The primary technology categories include Low Speed Coal Mills, Medium Speed Coal Mills, and High Speed Coal Mills, each tailored to distinct operational scales, throughput requirements, and coal properties.

